{% doc %}
  blocks/_featured-pills-step.liquid

  One card in a numbered sequence: a mark with a number pinned to it, and a
  sentence about what happens at that point. Three of them side by side are the
  *How it works* panel.

  ## Why it is not `blocks/badge-highlight.liquid`

  The Highlight tile is a mark, a heading and a line of text in a box, and it is
  the right block for three unordered benefits. This is an *ordered* set, and
  the order is the content: the number is not decoration on the card, it is what
  says this is the second of three and that the first one came before it.

  A tile with the number typed into the heading would leave the sequence
  invisible to a screen reader, unsortable by the merchant and out of step the
  moment a step is inserted in the middle. Here it is its own field, pinned to
  the mark by the stylesheet rather than by the copy, and it reads out as part
  of the card.

  Private — the leading underscore — because a step outside a sequence is a
  tile, and the theme already has one of those. It is addable inside a **Pill**
  and nowhere else.

  ## The mark is the theme's

  Shape, Ring and the icon colours are `snippets/icon-mark.liquid`: the same
  three groups with the same ids as the Feature icon, the Highlight tile and the
  pill in the strip above. The dotted ring the design draws is that snippet's
  `<circle>` with a round cap and no dash length — see the note there on why a
  dotted ring cannot be a `border`.

  ## The number sits on the ring, and the card does not grow to hold it

  It is absolutely positioned against the mark, which is the containing block,
  so the badge straddles the ring's edge without reserving a corner of the card
  for itself. A card whose height changes when a badge is switched on is a card
  that cannot be dropped into a row beside two that have not got one.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = block.settings

  assign has_icon = false
  if s.icon_source == 'icon' and s.icon != blank
    assign has_icon = true
  endif

  capture icon_px
    render 'icon-size', size: s.icon_size, custom: s.icon_size_custom
  endcapture
  assign icon_size = icon_px | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the frame ----

    Resolved the way every border in this theme is: `none` emits nothing at all,
    and with no colour picked the line is `currentColor` faded by `color-mix`,
    because the colour filters cannot take an alpha channel from a keyword.
  endcomment
  assign border_line = s.border_style | default: 'none'
  assign border_width = 0
  if border_line != 'none'
    assign border_width = s.border_width | default: 1 | plus: 0

    assign border_percent = s.border_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    if s.border_color == blank
      assign border_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ' | append: border_percent | append: '%, transparent)'
    else
      assign border_alpha = border_percent | divided_by: 100.0
      assign border_paint = s.border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', border_alpha
    endif
  endif

  comment
    Two properties, not one — `flex` only means anything to a flex item, and a
    step card is one only when the panel around it is a flex row. Fill is the
    default because a sequence is a row of equal cards, and a card sized to its
    own sentence makes the shortest step look like the least important one.
  endcomment
  assign width_pct = s.width_custom | default: 33 | plus: 0
  case s.width
    when 'fit'
      assign width_flex = '0 0 auto'
      assign width_size = 'fit-content'
    when 'custom'
      assign width_flex = '0 0 ' | append: width_pct | append: '%'
      assign width_size = width_pct | append: '%'
    else
      assign width_flex = '1 1 0%'
      assign width_size = '100%'
  endcase

  case s.alignment
    when 'start'
      assign align_axis = 'start'
      assign text_align = 'start'
    when 'end'
      assign align_axis = 'end'
      assign text_align = 'end'
    else
      assign align_axis = 'center'
      assign text_align = 'center'
  endcase

  assign preset = s.preset | default: 'default'
  assign heading_classes = 'featured-pills-step__heading block-text--' | append: preset
  if s.color == 'gradient'
    assign heading_classes = heading_classes | append: ' block-text--gradient'
  endif
-%}

{%- capture icon_mark_style -%}
  {%- render 'icon-mark', block: s, declarations: true -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture heading_style -%}
  {%- render 'block-typography', block: s -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture card_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', block: s, declarations: true -%}
  --fps-flex: {{ width_flex }};
  --fps-width: {{ width_size }};
  --fps-align: {{ align_axis }};
  --fps-text-align: {{ text_align }};
  --fps-gap: {{ s.gap | default: 16 | plus: 0 }}px;
  --fps-gap-mobile: {{ s.gap_mobile | default: s.gap | default: 16 | plus: 0 }}px;
  --fps-radius: {{ s.border_radius | default: 20 | plus: 0 }}px;
  --fps-border-width: {{ border_width }}px;
  {%- if border_width > 0 -%}
    --fps-border-style: {{ border_line }};
    --fps-border-color: {{ border_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.background != blank -%}
    --fps-background: {{ s.background }};
  {%- endif -%}
  --fps-text-size: {{ s.text_size | default: 15 | plus: 0 | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
  {%- if s.text_color != blank -%}
    --fps-text-color: {{ s.text_color }};
  {%- endif -%}
  --fps-number-size: {{ s.number_size | default: 22 | plus: 0 }}px;
  {%- if s.number_background != blank -%}
    --fps-number-background: {{ s.number_background }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.number_color != blank -%}
    --fps-number-color: {{ s.number_color }};
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<div
  class="featured-pills-step icon-mark-host"
  data-block-spacing
  style="{{ card_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- if has_icon -%}
    <span class="featured-pills-step__mark icon-mark" aria-hidden="true" style="{{ icon_mark_style | strip_newlines | strip }}">
      {% render 'icon-mark', block: s %}
      {% render 'icon', icon: s.icon, size: icon_size %}

      {%- comment -%}
        Inside the mark rather than beside it, because the mark is the box the
        badge is positioned against. Not `aria-hidden`: the number is the step's
        place in the sequence and reads out with the rest of the card — the
        `aria-hidden` on the mark itself covers only the glyph and the ring,
        which are decoration, so the badge carries `aria-hidden="false"` back.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if s.number != blank -%}
        <span class="featured-pills-step__number" aria-hidden="false">{{ s.number | escape }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
  {%- elsif s.number != blank -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      A step with no glyph still has a number, and with no mark to pin it to it
      becomes the mark. Same element, same settings, drawn on its own.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <span class="featured-pills-step__number featured-pills-step__number--alone">{{ s.number | escape }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}

  <span class="featured-pills-step__body">
    {%- if s.heading != blank -%}
      <span class="{{ heading_classes }}" style="{{ heading_style | strip_newlines | strip }}">
        {{- s.heading | escape -}}
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.text != blank -%}
      <span class="featured-pills-step__text">{{ s.text }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </span>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  Every setting below is a control a merchant reaches in the editor, and the
  schema is one element's styling surface: splitting it to get under Theme
  Check's count of 40 would split the thing the settings style.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% # theme-check-disable ExcessiveSettingsCount %}
